Killing a peaceful costs more alignment points than killing
a hostile earns I think.  By the late game there are so many
more hostiles than peacefuls it no longer matters, but in the
early game like the mines it does matter.

Since alignment matters at prayer, you'll want to target
"stridently aligned" yet it's hard to know without a wand in
enlightenment.  One simple way is to keep a count of
hostiles you've killed.  If you only kill 1 peaceful for every 5
hostiles as you go, kill all you like for their stuff and the XP
points.  Excepting the ones with good reasons to avoid.  The
1-to-5 ratio is probably overkill and does not take exact
points per monster into account, but it's easy.  By the time
I'm past Sokoban I no longer count at all.  By that point the
number of hostiles is so much larger than the number of
peacefuls it stops mattering.


